<title>FRANCE: French watchdog approves SEP offer terms.</title>
<headline>French watchdog approves SEP offer terms.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French Financial Markets Committee said on Thursday an offer by aero-engine maker Snecma to buy out minority shareholders in rocket motor firm SEP at 625 francs per share was acceptable.</p>
<p>The committee said in a statement that Banque Arjil, acting for Snecma, had valued SEP at between 519 and 658 francs per share on a multi-criteria analysis. A cashflow analysis narrowed the valuation to 622 and 631 francs per share.</p>
<p>Based on the studies, Snecma is offering 625 francs. &quot;The (committee) board declared it acceptable,&quot; the committee said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452 pnt/cla</p>
</text>
